2. Stellar Settlement Infrastructure


2.1 Deposit Attribution Engine


Because opening a dedicated Stellar account per invoice incurs base reserve overhead (minimum account balance in XLM), WigglePay uses Attribution via Multiplexed Accounts (MED25519) and fallback 64-bit Memo IDs:


* Multiplexed Account Routing: WigglePay generates an M-address encoding the merchant’s base account and a unique 64-bit Invoice Sub-ID.
* Memo Fallback: For wallets lacking multiplexed support, an explicit Memo-Text or Memo-ID is assigned and strictly validated.
* Asset Scope: Supports native XLM, standard stablecoins (e.g., USDC issued by Centre/Circle on Stellar), and platform-custom merchant loyalty tokens.
Path Payments: Incorporates Stellar Path Payments so payers can settle using arbitrary assets (e.g., native XLM) while the merchant receives their desired asset (e.g., USDC), resolved at the protocol level through the Stellar Decentralized Exchange (SDEX).


2.2 Payment Listener Architecture


A dedicated, long-running daemon process continuously monitors the Stellar Horizon streaming endpoint (/accounts/{account_id}/payments via Server-Sent Events):


* Event Ingestion: Horizon SSE pushes incoming transaction envelopes in real time.
* Idempotency Gate: Hashes transaction identifiers (tx_hash) into Redis using an atomic lock to eliminate double-crediting.
* Ledger Validation: The daemon extracts the destination address, asset, amount, and memo/multiplexed ID, cross-referencing open invoices.
* State Transition: The invoice status transitions from PENDING to SETTLED. A signal emitted across Redis Pub/Sub triggers:
   * WebSocket broadcast to the React payment modal.
   * Live stream overlay triggers (audio alerts, on-screen animations).
   * Instant Telegram notification sent back to the merchant.
Outbound HTTP Webhooks dispatched to the merchant's endpoint.


3. Backend Architecture (Django & DRF)


3.1 Core Domain Models


* Merchant: Stores Stellar public keys (destination accounts), webhook URLs, signing secrets, commission rates, and widget configurations.
* Invoice: Contains UUID, merchant pointer, asset code, expected amount, settled amount, memo identifier, multiplexed address, status (DRAFT, PENDING, SETTLED, EXPIRED, CANCELLED), and expiry timestamp.
* WidgetConfig: Manages display options, custom input fields (payer name, message, tip presets), webhook mappings, and live stream overlays.
* TransactionRecord: Logs Stellar transaction hash, ledger index, sender address, gas fee paid, and routing path.
TelegramProfile: Maps merchant foreign keys, Telegram chat IDs, authorization levels, and conversational state context.


3.2 Asynchronous Worker Topology (Celery + Redis)


* Queue 1 (stellar_queue): Handles high-priority ledger verification, path payment calculations, and transaction validation.
* Queue 2 (ai_queue): Executes audio decoding, voice note speech-to-text processing, and LLM structured information extraction.
Queue 3 (webhook_queue): Dispatches merchant notifications using exponential backoff and HMAC-SHA256 request signatures.


3.3 Containerized Architecture (Docker Composition)


The deployment is split into distinct, single-responsibility containers configured via Docker Compose:




