7.2 Embeddable Widget Layout Architecture


Container Components & Styling Rules


* Container: Fixed dimension container (max-width 420px) with automatic vertical centering.
* Top Header: Displays merchant avatar/branding lockup, payment title, and active currency selector.
* Body Area: Segmented toggle switching between Direct Wallet Connect (Freighter/Albedo) and Manual Transfer (QR Code + Address/Memo).
* Dynamic Display: Monospace typography for public Stellar keys and M-addresses with quick-copy actions.
Action Footer: Primary full-width CTA button alongside platform trust badge ("Powered by Stellar Network").


Responsive Breakpoints


* Small (< 480px): Full-viewport bottom sheet; touch targets expand to minimum 48px.
Desktop (> 768px): Centered floating dialog with animated modal transitions.


Interaction & State Machine Transitions


* IDLE: Displays invoice details and asset requirements.
* SIGNING: Disables controls and presents visual indicators waiting for wallet signature.
* BROADCASTING: Displays pulsing progression state indicating ledger ingestion.
* SUCCESS: Transitions to checkmark view with transaction proof link.
* ERROR / EXPIRED: Presents explicit error details with a quick "Regenerate Invoice" action.
8. Security, Fault Tolerance, & System Features
8. Security, Fault Tolerance, and Value-Add Specifications
8.1 Transaction Security & Replay Prevention
8.1 Transaction Security & Replay Prevention


* Replay Protection: Enforces a database uniqueness constraint on TransactionRecord.tx_hash. The Horizon listener automatically rejects previously credited hashes.
* Underpayment & Overpayment Handling:
   * Underpayment: Invoice transitions to PARTIALLY_PAID; widget prompts for remaining balance.
   * Overpayment: Invoice marked SETTLED; excess balance is credited with an automated refund flag.
8.2 API Developer Experience
8.2 API Developer Experience


* HMAC Request Signatures: Every outbound webhook payload is signed using SHA256 HMAC in the X-WigglePay-Signature header.
* REST Endpoints for Integrations:
   * POST /api/v1/invoices/: Programmatic invoice creation.
   * GET /api/v1/invoices/{id}/: Invoice query and settlement status verification.
   * POST /api/v1/widgets/: Remote configuration of embedded payment links.
8.3 Value-Add System Features
8.3 Value-Add Architecture Features


* Dynamic Slippage Management for Path Payments: The widget queries real-time conversion quotes from Horizon APIs, locking price guarantees for 60 seconds to protect against asset volatility during payment execution.
* Zero-Config OBS Alerts: Streamers paste a single URL into OBS Studio; configuration edits instantly update live overlay layouts via WebSockets without requiring broadcast restarts.
Automated Payout Splitting (Soroban Extension): Future-proof smart contract integration permitting secondary routing (e.g., 95% merchant payout, 5% platform fee) via non-custodial Soroban escrow contracts.